                <pb facs="1478" n="1464" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 LCC/29: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-22T22:00:00+03:00">June 22, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 23—7:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2236. Department’s 1495, June 15, 6 p.m. The British Ambassador has telegraphed
                    the British Foreign Office that the functions of the <pb facs="1479" n="1465"
                        xml:id="pg1465"/> LPC had already been explained to a Soviet official
                    subsequent to the receipt of the Soviet reply agreeing to participation therein.
                    The Ambassador stated that he preferred not to raise the question with the
                    Soviets again until he has received a reply to his letter to Molotov of June 1
                    in which he had requested the names of the proposed members of the LPC and the
                    nomination of some Soviet official in Moscow with whom the appropriate member of
                    the British Embassy could deal. In view of the foregoing neither the British nor
                    ourselves are taking any further action here at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
